Making Exported Variables Permanent

Variables exported in the command line are temporary and disappear the moment you close your terminal window. To make them persist permanently across restarts and new sessions(new terminal or new shell), you must add the export command to your shell's configuration files:

• For your specific user account: Append the export statement to your user profile file, usually ~/.bashrc or ~/.bash_profile.

echo 'export MY_PERMANENT_VAR="value"' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc  # Reloads the file so it takes effect immediately

